  "id": "jumping-stand",
  "term": "jumping stand",
  "definition": "A jumping stand is a behavioral testing apparatus used in discrimination and visual perception tasks in which an animal jumps from an elevated starting point toward one of two targets. Correct choices lead to a safe landing and reward, while incorrect choices lead to an immediate negative outcome, making it a way to study learning and stimulus-guided responding.",
